  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on comparing the variances of the two lotteries and preferring the one with the smaller variance. Lottery A offers 500 Euros with 100% probability, so its variance is 0 (since there is no deviation from the outcome). Lottery B offers 1000 Euros with 50% probability and 0 Euros with 50% probability, so its expected value is 500 Euros, and its variance is (1000 - 500)^2 * 0.5 + (0 - 500)^2 * 0.5 = 250,000. Thus, Lottery A has a smaller variance than Lottery B. The decision reason would therefore prefer Lottery A. The relevant information (variances) can be derived from the given probabilities and outcomes, so the reason can be applied to the decision problem.",
